      "question": "What embedding model does GraphRAG++ use and what dimension are the vectors?",
      "ground_truth": "GraphRAG++ uses BAAI/bge-m3 as the default embedding model, which produces 1024-dimensional vectors. This replaced the previous all-MiniLM-L6-v2 model (384-dim) to improve retrieval quality from an MTEB score of approximately 56 to approximately 70.",
